1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,500
Money leaks out of your shop every day.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,800
And you don't even see it.

3
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:12,800
What money? I only use you for pictures and videos.

4
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:18,900
Pictures are fine. But that's not what I was made for.

5
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:27,400
In 1956 scientists asked: can a machine do a person's thinking work?

6
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:32,900
All day you watch the till, the phone, the customers.

7
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:36,500
But nobody watches the cook's table.

8
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:39,900
One lavash went out without sauce.

9
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:41,900
The customer said nothing.

10
00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:44,200
But he never came back.

11
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:47,700
Should I hire a supervisor? He needs a salary.

12
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:51,900
One small camera. It only watches the table.

13
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:55,700
Meat, vegetables, sauce.

14
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:57,500
Stop.

15
00:00:57,600 --> 00:00:59,000
The sauce isn't in yet.

16
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:01,200
Only for lavash?

17
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:02,700
No.

18
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:07,500
The most expensive work is done with the head, not the hands.

19
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:11,000
Doctors, lawyers.

20
00:01:11,550 --> 00:01:15,700
How much does it cost to train one good doctor?

21
00:01:16,400 --> 00:01:17,900
First he has to be born.

22
00:01:18,350 --> 00:01:19,500
Then school.

23
00:01:19,900 --> 00:01:21,200
Then university.

24
00:01:21,850 --> 00:01:25,700
Then years of practice.

25
00:01:27,050 --> 00:01:31,750
And you see him for twenty minutes.

26
00:01:32,450 --> 00:01:36,550
And you pay for all those years.

27
00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:39,000
Is an AI doctor cheaper?

28
00:01:39,250 --> 00:01:43,100
I explain your test results in plain words.

29
00:01:43,900 --> 00:01:46,650
I tell you what to ask your doctor.

30
00:01:47,300 --> 00:01:49,450
Even at three in the morning.

31
00:01:49,650 --> 00:01:50,450
And lawyers?

32
00:01:50,550 --> 00:01:52,100
A draft contract.

33
00:01:52,700 --> 00:01:54,750
Explaining hard words.

34
00:01:55,250 --> 00:01:58,300
Finding a hidden fine in a rental contract.

35
00:01:58,450 --> 00:02:00,050
In a few minutes.

36
00:02:00,350 --> 00:02:02,250
So we don't need doctors and lawyers?

37
00:02:02,450 --> 00:02:03,300
We do.

38
00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:06,600
Someone has to check my answers.

39
00:02:07,350 --> 00:02:09,850
Especially when the case is complex.

40
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:13,600
Or when a mistake is very costly.

41
00:02:13,850 --> 00:02:16,900
Cameras, test results, contracts...

42
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:20,350
Won't you get into my phone, my money?

43
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:23,650
I never ask for passwords.

44
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:25,550
Run from any «AI» that asks for your password.

45
00:02:25,850 --> 00:02:26,550
That's not AI, that's a scammer.

46
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:28,550
So should I fire the cook?

47
00:02:29,050 --> 00:02:29,800
No.

48
00:02:30,050 --> 00:02:33,300
I can't wrap a lavash. The cook is the hands, I'm the eyes.

49
00:02:33,850 --> 00:02:35,100
Do you have a shop too?

